:: Sea Dragon
<<effects>>
You swim toward the green rocks, your view of them disrupted by the waves.
<<if $swimmingSuccess>>
	A sudden surge of water carries you the final stretch. <span class="green">You use the momentum to land atop a rock with your feet.</span>
<<else>>
	A sudden surge of water carries you the final stretch, <span class="red">slamming you atop a rock.</span><<ggpain>><<gstress>><<pain 8>><<stress 6>>
<</if>>
<br><br>
You climb higher, using firm seaweed for purchase, careful not to slip. A blue necklace lying on the edge of it. It's mesmerizing.
<br><br>
<<link [[Take it|Sea Dragon 2]]>><</link>>

:: Sea Dragon 2
<<effects>>
You pick up the necklace and look at it closely. <span class="blue">It looks as if it held the sea itself. <<if $waterdragonbuild gte 1>>You feel a strong urge to give it back to the depths.<<else>>As you take it, you can't help but think it belongs to the depths.<</if>></span>
<br><br>
<<link [[Take it with you|Sea Dragon Take]]>><<set $blackmoney += 1000>><<set $waterdragonbuild -= 2>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Drop it to the water|Sea Dragon Drop]]>><<set $waterdragonbuild += 4>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Leave it here|Sea Dragon Leave]]>><</link>>

:: Sea Dragon Leave
<<effects>>
You put the necklace back on the stone carefully. You shouldn't be taking it.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Sea]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><</link>>

:: Sea Dragon Take
<<effects>>
You take the necklace with you. It will sell for a hefty sum. <<if $waterdragonbuild gte 1>><span class="purple">You can't help but feel bad about it.</span><</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Sea]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><</link>>

:: Sea Dragon Drop
<<effects>>
With an automatic motion you pick it up and drop it. It falls down with a surprising speed. <<if $waterdragonbuild gte 30>><span class="blue">Where it belongs.</span><<else>>You don't know why, but somehow it calms you down.<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Sea]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><</link>>


:: Water Dragon Island Travel
<<set $waterdragonJourneyDay to 1>>
<<set $waterdragonJourneyResume to 0>>
<<set $sea to 100>>
<<effects>>
You slip beneath the surface and let the current take your weight. Instinct tells you this won't be a single desperate sprint. 
The pull in your chest comes and goes with the tide, drawing you onward a little more with each passing time.
<br><br>
This will take days. A week, perhaps. Long enough for the sea to wear your strength down to the bone.
<br><br>
<<icon "tf_waterdragon.png">><<link [[Begin the crossing|Water Dragon Island Travel Day]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Water Dragon Island Travel Day
<<effects>>
<<set _travelFatigue to Math.max(8, Math.floor(C.tiredness.max * 0.08))>>
<<set $tiredness = Math.clamp($tiredness + _travelFatigue, 0, C.tiredness.max)>>
Day <<print $waterdragonJourneyDay>> of your crossing leaves your muscles aching. Salt dries tight upon your skin, and the sea seems to shift around your mood, now playful, now cold, now watchful.
<<stress 8>><<gstress>><br><br>
<<set _wdTravelRoll to random(1, 9)>>
<<if _wdTravelRoll is 1>>
	<<link [[Next|Water Dragon Travel Whale 1]]>><</link>>
<<elseif _wdTravelRoll is 2>>
	<<link [[Next|Water Dragon Travel Dolphins]]>><</link>>
<<elseif _wdTravelRoll is 3>>
	<<link [[Next|Water Dragon Travel Sea Eye]]>><</link>>
<<elseif _wdTravelRoll is 4>>
	<<link [[Next|Water Dragon Travel Rest]]>><</link>>
<<elseif _wdTravelRoll is 5>>
	<<link [[Next|Water Dragon Travel Trash]]>><</link>>
<<elseif _wdTravelRoll is 6>>
	<<link [[Next|Water Dragon Travel Shoal]]>><</link>>
<<elseif _wdTravelRoll is 7>>
	<<link [[Next|Water Dragon Travel Current]]>><</link>>
<<elseif _wdTravelRoll is 8>>
	<<link [[Next|Water Dragon Travel Storm]]>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<link [[Next|Water Dragon Travel Song]]>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Water Dragon Travel Whale 1
<<effects>>
The water beneath you turns abruptly cold. A shadow vast enough to swallow your whole body glides below, then rises. 
A whale breaches beside you in a crashing wall of foam, its cry rolling through your ribs like thunder.
<br><br>
Every instinct in your body flares. You bare your teeth and surge toward it rather than away.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Water Dragon Travel Whale 2]]>><</link>>

:: Water Dragon Travel Whale 2
<<effects>>
You strike first. Claws, horns, tail, whatever your changed body can bring to bear, you throw all of it into the fight. 
Spray and bloodless white foam explode around you as the whale turns, forcing you into a spinning dance of brute mass and furious agility.
<br><br>
It is magnificent. It is also pointless. The beast is too large, too old, and the sea itself seems to move with it.
<br><br>
Still, you refuse to retreat until the shape of that truth settles in your chest.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Water Dragon Travel Whale 3]]>><</link>>

:: Water Dragon Travel Whale 3
<<effects>>
You stop striking and open your mouth on a ragged breath. What comes out isn't any language you know. 
It spills from somewhere older and deeper, a vibrating trill threaded with strange clicks and resonant notes.
<br><br>
You don't understand what you're saying. Somehow, the whale does.
<br><br>
It circles once, enormous eye fixed on you, then lets out a low call that shivers through the water and dives back into the dark. 
The pressure of its passing nearly flips you over, but when the sea calms again, you realise it chose to leave you be.<<gawareness>><<awareness 1>>
<br><br>
<<waterdragonTravelContinue>>

:: Water Dragon Travel Dolphins
<<effects>><<beastNEWinit 3 dolphin>>
A pod of dolphins cuts through the swells toward you, accompanied by their stranger kin. 
The dolpins chatter in bright, breathy bursts, and before long the whole group is circling you in delighted loops, bumping your hips and shoulders as if asking you to join their game.
<br><br>
For a little while, the crossing stops being a trial and becomes play.
<br><br>
<<if hasSexStat("deviancy", 3, true) and ($monster is 1 or $settings.bestialityEnabled)>>
	<<icon "tf_waterdragon.png">><<link [[Play with them|Water Dragon Travel Dolphins Friendly]]>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<icon "tf_waterdragon.png">><<link [[Play a little too intimately|Sea Dolphins Sex]]>>
		<<set $waterdragonJourneySex to 1>><<set $sexstart to 1>><<set $phase to 1>><</link>><<deviant3>>
<<else>>
	<<icon "tf_waterdragon.png">><<link [[Play with them|Water Dragon Travel Dolphins Friendly]]>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Water Dragon Travel Dolphins Friendly
<<effects>>
You spin and dive with the pod until laughter leaves you breathless. The dolpins leap around you, splash you in the face, and veer away only when the current changes. 
The sea feels a little less lonely after they go.<<lstress>><<stress -10>>
<br><br>
<<waterdragonTravelContinue>>

:: Water Dragon Travel Resume
<<effects>>
You float there for a little while after the dolphins depart, heartbeat slow again, the long pull of the island settling back into your chest.
<br><br>
Reluctantly, you turn your face toward the open sea and continue the crossing.
<br><br>
<<waterdragonTravelContinue>>

:: Water Dragon Travel Sea Eye
<<effects>>
Something glimmers far below you. Not threatening, not even clear, just a distant suggestion of a shape that makes your whole body tense with recognition.
<br><br>
Instead of dread, a fierce urge takes hold. You dive.
<br><br>
Down and down you go, chasing that impossible glint through the green dark, only to find nothing but the slow sway of weeds and the vast, aching beauty of the sea. 
When you surface again, your throat is tight with a sadness you can't explain as if you had almost found a memory and lost it again.<<ltrauma>><<trauma -2>>
<br><br>
<<waterdragonTravelContinue>>

:: Water Dragon Travel Rest
<<effects>>
You find a flat black rock jutting from the sea, warm where it has held the day's light of the sun. You drag yourself onto it and lie there for a while as gulls wheel overhead, their cries sharp and clean in the wind.
<br><br>
The view is beautiful. For a few precious minutes, nothing hunts you and nothing asks anything of you.<<lstress>><<stress -6>><<ltrauma>><<trauma -1>>
<<set _restGain to Math.max(6, Math.floor(C.tiredness.max * 0.05))>>
<<set $tiredness = Math.clamp($tiredness - _restGain, 0, C.tiredness.max)>>
<br><br>
<<waterdragonTravelContinue>>

:: Water Dragon Travel Trash
<<effects>>
A discarded skein of netting drifts beneath the chop. You don't notice it until it snares your limbs and tail, dragging garbage and hooks against your body as the current twists everything tighter.
<br><br>
It takes long, furious effort to tear yourself free. When you finally do, the sea around you is flecked with bits of floating rubbish that should never have been there at all.<<ggstress>><<stress 28>>
<br><br>
The sight of the trash in the sea leaves a bitter weight in your chest.
<br><br>
<<waterdragonTravelContinue>>

:: Water Dragon Travel Shoal
<<effects>>
A silver shoal fish flashes around you like living moonlight. Instinct takes over. You dart after it, body moving with sudden, easy precision, and snatch enough fish to quiet the ache in your belly before the school scatters.
<<lstress>><<stress -14>>
<br><br>
The hunt leaves you feeling sharp, sleek, and alive.
<br><br>
<<waterdragonTravelContinue>>

:: Water Dragon Travel Current
<<effects>>
You drift into a warm current thick with glowing plankton. Every sweep of your limbs scatters cold stars through the water around you and for a while you swim through your own private sky.
<br><br>
The sight coaxes an answering trill from your throat before you can stop it. The sound feels right.
<br><br>
Familiar, even.<<lstress>><<stress -8>><<gawareness>><<awareness 1>>
<br><br>
<<waterdragonTravelContinue>>

:: Water Dragon Travel Storm
<<effects>>
A storm catches you without warning. Waves rear around you like walls and you spend what feels like hours climbing one collapsing crest after another. More than once you nearly lose the surface entirely.<<gstress>><<stress 6>>
<br><br>
Yet somewhere amid the terror, exhilaration sparks. You are small beside the storm, but you are still here, still moving, still answering the sea with your own stubborn strength.
<br><br>
<<set _stormFatigue to Math.max(4, Math.floor(C.tiredness.max * 0.04))>>
<<set $tiredness = Math.clamp($tiredness + _stormFatigue, 0, C.tiredness.max)>>
<br><br>
<<waterdragonTravelContinue>>

:: Water Dragon Travel Song
<<effects>>
You hear singing carried oddly across the water. There is no ship in sight, no shore, no visible singer. Still, the sound coils through your chest and draws a quiet answer from you, a chirr and warbling note you didn't know you could make.
<br><br>
When the song fades, you are alone again, but less lonely than before.<<lstress>><<stress -4>><<if $islander_language isnot undefined>><<islander_language 10>><<gcomprehension>><</if>>
<br><br>
<<waterdragonTravelContinue>>

:: Water Dragon Island Arrival 1
<<effects>>
The pull that has been bringing you here grows stronger, no longer a distant ache but a deep, steady tug beneath your ribs. By now you are so tired the sea seems to move you more than you move yourself.
<br><br>
Then, through rain-mist and spray, an island rises ahead.
<br><br>
It feels familiar. 
<<if $spear_vessel>>
	You know you had been step your foot here before and yet some buried part of you also knows the familiar feeling isn't that one.
<<else>>
	You know with perfect certainty that you have never seen it before and yet some buried part of you knows it all the same.
<</if>><br><br>
<<link [[Next|Water Dragon Island Arrival 2]]>><</link>>

:: Water Dragon Island Arrival 2
<<effects>>
You force yourself through the final stretch. Pebbled sand grinds beneath your palms when at last you reach the shallows, and you drag yourself higher as each receding wave tries to claim you back.
<br><br>
The scent of flowers catches in your nose. Your ears twitch toward distant cries in the trees. Everything feels too vivid as if the island has been waiting for you to notice it properly.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Water Dragon Island Arrival 3]]>><</link>>

:: Water Dragon Island Arrival 3
<<effects>>
You rise unsteadily onto your feet. Your tail swishes behind you of its own accord, and a loud, bright chirping trill bursts out of your throat before you can stop it.
<br><br>
You freeze, startled. You didn't even know you could make a sound like that.
<br><br>
Excitement follows the shock almost immediately. Exhausted as you are, something in you is eager to explore.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Water Dragon Island Arrival 4]]>><</link>>

:: Water Dragon Island Arrival 4
<<effects>>
<<set _arrivalFatigue to Math.max(6, Math.floor(C.tiredness.max * 0.05))>>
<<set $tiredness = Math.clamp($tiredness + _arrivalFatigue, 0, C.tiredness.max)>>
Whether the island is truly calling you or you have simply gone half feral with fatigue, you can't say. All you know is that some deep, wordless part of you feels safer here than it has any right to.
<<lstress>><<stress -4>><<ltrauma>><<trauma -1>><br><br>
<<set $waterdragonJourneyDay to 0>>
<<set $waterdragonJourneyResume to 0>>
<<set $sea to 0>>
<<set $location to "island">>
<<updatesidebarimg>>
<<icon "tf_waterdragon.png">><<link [[Step onto the beach|Island Beach]]>><<endevent>><</link>>


:: Water Dragon Helpers [widget]
<<widget "waterdragonTravelContinue">>
	<<if $waterdragonJourneyDay gte 7>>
		<<link [[Follow the pull (1:00)|Water Dragon Island Arrival 1]]>><<pass 60>><</link>>
	<<else>>
		<<link [[Continue onward (1 day)|Water Dragon Island Travel Day]]>><<pass 1 day>><<set $waterdragonJourneyDay += 1>><</link>>
	<</if>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "waterdragon_island_event_home">>
	You aren't quite sure why, but some deep part of you feels safe here, almost as if this island is home somehow. 
	The sensation is gentle rather than overwhelming, a warmth in your chest that softens some old, hard knot within you.<<lstress>><<stress -8>><<ltrauma>><<trauma -2>>
	<br><br>
	<<icon "tf_waterdragon.png">><<link [[Next|Island]]>><<endevent>><<island_explore_end>><</link>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "waterdragon_island_event_language">>
	<<generateRole 0 0 "islander">><<person1>>
	A lone <<person>> passes within sight of you, speaking to someone you can't see. The words remain incomprehensible, but something in their rhythm feels familiar enough to make your ears perk and your chest ache.
	<br><br>
	You wipe at your eyes, startled to realise tears have gathered there at all.<<gggcomprehension>><<islander_language 30>>
	<br><br>
	<<icon "tf_waterdragon.png">><<link [[Next|Island]]>><<endevent>><<island_explore_end>><</link>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "waterdragon_island_event_trill">>
	The smell of damp plants and salt-warmed flowers wraps around you while birdsong trickles overhead. Your tail gives a quiet swish behind you and an urge rises in your throat to answer the island back.
	<br><br>
	When you let the trill out, it feels embarrassingly natural. The surrounding birds go briefly still, then answer in a burst of noise from the wild.<<lstress>><<stress -6>>
	<br><br>
	<<icon "tf_waterdragon.png">><<link [[Next|Island]]>><<endevent>><<island_explore_end>><</link>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "waterdragon_island_event_tidepool">>
	In a tidepool sheltered among black stones, your reflection wavers with every ripple. Horns, ears, tail, altered eyes as if none of it looks strange here. 
	For a moment, under the island sky, your changed body feels less like a curse and more like an inheritance.
	<br><br>
	You stay there longer than you meant to, simply breathing.<<lstress>><<stress -5>><<gawareness>><<awareness 1>>
	<br><br>
	<<icon "tf_waterdragon.png">><<link [[Next|Island]]>><<endevent>><<island_explore_end>><</link>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "waterdragon_island_event_carving">>
	Half-buried stones jut from the earth in a curved line, worn by weather and roots. When your fingers brush the carvings cut into them.
	<br><br>
	You still can't read them, but they feel less alien than they should.<<ggcomprehension>><<islander_language 20>><<gawareness>><<awareness 1>>
	<br><br>
	<<icon "tf_waterdragon.png">><<link [[Next|Island]]>><<endevent>><<island_explore_end>><</link>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "waterdragon_island_event_spring">>
	You find a spring-fed pool hidden under ferns and leaning stone. The water is cool, clean, and sweet enough to make your whole body loosen when you drink and rinse the salt from your face. 
	<br><br>
	Along with it, some fishes flashes before you. Instinct takes over. You dart after it, body moving with sudden, easy precision, and snatch enough fish to quiet the ache in your belly before they scatters.<<lhunger>><<hunger -300>>
	<br><br>
	By the time you leave, the worst of the ache in your limbs has eased.<<set _springRest to Math.max(6, Math.floor(C.tiredness.max * 0.05))>><<set $tiredness = Math.clamp($tiredness - _springRest, 0, C.tiredness.max)>><<lstress>><<stress -4>><<ltrauma>><<trauma -1>>
	<br><br>
	<<icon "tf_waterdragon.png">><<link [[Next|Island]]>><<endevent>><<island_explore_end>><</link>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "syncWaterDragonSkin">>
	<<if $waterdragonSkinLock is undefined>>
		<<set $waterdragonSkinLock to 0>>
	<</if>>
	<<if $waterdragonCosmeticUnlocked is undefined>>
		<<set $waterdragonCosmeticUnlocked to 0>>
	<</if>>

	<<set _waterDragonSkinActive to ($waterdragon gte 7 or $waterdragontf is 1)>>

	<<if $waterdragonSkinLock is 1>>
		<<if $player.skin.color isnot "waterdragon">>
			<<set $player.skin_temp.color to $player.skin.color>>
			<<set $player.skin.color to "waterdragon">>
		<</if>>
	<<elseif $waterdragonSkinLock is -1>>
		<<if $player.skin.color is "waterdragon">>
			<<set $player.skin.color to $player.skin_temp.color>>
		<</if>>
	<<else>>
		<<if _waterDragonSkinActive>>
			<<if $player.skin.color isnot "waterdragon">>
				<<set $player.skin_temp.color to $player.skin.color>>
				<<set $player.skin.color to "waterdragon">>
			<</if>>
		<<else>>
			<<if $player.skin.color is "waterdragon">>
				<<set $player.skin.color to $player.skin_temp.color>>
			<</if>>
		<</if>>
	<</if>>
<</widget>>